{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 254613, "name": "D Essin", "username": "f0cd9c5c9c9e24f57bd0518bec905b6", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-11-10T20:47:13.244Z", "cooked": "<p>Since the upgrade, Every  time I launch any terminal I get error “egrep: warning: egrep is obsolescent; using grep -E”</p>\n<p>It appares first, the the prompt is displayed on the next line in any new terminal window</p>\n<p>There are no references to egrep in either ,bashrc, .profile, or .zshrc</p>\n<p>Why am I suddenly getting this message? I can’t see why invoking a terminal app would have anything to do with any kind of grep</p>\n<p>How do I eliminate it?</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-10T21:12:18.664Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1035, "reads": 42, "readers_count": 41, "score": 5183.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "D Essin", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4017, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254618, "name": "Chris Williams", "username": "chrisawi", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/eb7434/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-11-10T21:05:30.759Z", "cooked": "<p>On my system (F39 Silverblue), egrep is an alias. Only when I delete that alias do I see that warning from <code>/usr/bin/egrep</code>. The alias is defined in <code>/etc/profile.d/colorgrep.sh</code>.</p>\n<p>What shell are you using? You mentioned both .bashrc and .zshrc</p>\n<p>Assuming bash, does it appear again if you run <code>bash</code> inside the shell? If so, try <code>bash -x</code> to trace it.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-10T21:05:30.759Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 38, "readers_count": 37, "score": 27.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "Chris Williams", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16855, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254621, "name": "Barry A Scott", "username": "barryascott", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/db3279/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-11-10T21:11:56.488Z", "cooked": "<p>Search in /etc for a file that uses egrep.<br>\nLikely something in /etc/profile.d I would suspect.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-10T21:11:56.488Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 35, "readers_count": 34, "score": 22.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "Barry A Scott", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Building the Outer Ring (Copr Build VI)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4115, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/3", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254646, "name": "Jeff V", "username": "computersavvy", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/computersavvy/{size}/4741_2.png", "created_at": "2023-11-11T00:09:46.050Z", "cooked": "<p>Anything that uses the egrep command directly will receive that warning.  /usr/bin/egrep is a shell script as shown here.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\"># file /usr/bin/egrep\n/usr/bin/egrep: a /usr/bin/sh script, ASCII text executable\n\n\n# cat /usr/bin/egrep\n#!/usr/bin/sh\ncmd=${0##*/}\necho \"$cmd: warning: $cmd is obsolescent; using grep -E\" &gt;&amp;2\nexec grep -E \"$@\"\n</code></pre>\n<p>so calling that command produces the message before actually calling grep.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-11T19:24:31.668Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 28, "readers_count": 27, "score": 40.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "Jeff V", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Q&A Leader", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 3019, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254649, "name": "D Essin", "username": "f0cd9c5c9c9e24f57bd0518bec905b6", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-11-11T01:49:47.258Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"chrisawi\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"95602\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/eb7434/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chris Williams:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What shell are you using? You mentioned both .bashrc and .zshrc</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’m using zsh but a web search suggested looking in those other files, so I looked and didn;t find grep or egrep in any oy them.</p>\n<p>I have made the edits that were suggested.</p>\n<p>Thank you</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-11T01:49:47.258Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 40.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "D Essin", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4017, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254656, "name": "Chris Williams", "username": "chrisawi", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/eb7434/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-11-11T02:18:13.644Z", "cooked": "<p>zsh has a similar tracing feature. You can try <code>zsh -x |&amp; grep egrep</code></p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-11T02:18:13.644Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 5, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 30.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "Chris Williams", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 4017, "username": "f0cd9c5c9c9e24f57bd0518bec905b6", "name": "D Essin", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/294172/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16855, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254720, "name": "Michael J Gruber", "username": "mjg", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/mjg/{size}/643_2.png", "created_at": "2023-11-11T12:03:04.898Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"computersavvy\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"95602\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/computersavvy/48/4741_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeff V:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Anything that uses the egrep command directly will receive that warning.  /usr/bin/egrep is a shell script as shown here.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\"># file /usr/bin/egrep\n/usr/bin/egrep: a /usr/bin/sh script, ASCII text executable\n\n\n# cat /usr/bin/egrep\n#!/usr/bin/sh\ncmd=${0##*/}\necho \"$cmd: warning: $cmd is obsolescent; using grep -E\" &gt;&amp;2\nexec grep -E \"$@\"\n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, that one is super annoying, because it bugs the user without any hint on the root cause. If it was meant to be useful it should have included <code>$PPID</code> or <code>$(pstree $PPID)</code> in its output (or even higher up the dependency tree).</p>\n<p>The alias <code>egrep 'grep -E --color=auto'</code>, while being useful, is a double bummer, because it trains people to use <code>egrep</code>, and once they write that in their scripts it depends on the presence of the alias.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-11T12:03:04.898Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 14, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 73.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "Michael J Gruber", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Adult Frog", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 3019, "username": "computersavvy", "name": "Jeff V", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/computersavvy/{size}/4741_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 663, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}, {"id": "totally", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 254820, "name": "D Essin", "username": "f0cd9c5c9c9e24f57bd0518bec905b6", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-11-11T18:46:06.677Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for this useful explanation</p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-11-11T18:46:06.677Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 5, "reads": 15, "readers_count": 14, "score": 28.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 95602, "topic_slug": "more-39-problems-egrep-warning", "display_username": "D Essin", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4017, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/more-39-problems-egrep-warning/95602/8", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, 